      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"advanced or unauthorized space mission activity\" is a pretty big understatement if it's happening that consistently. i was thinking about the interval... 6 minutes and 14 seconds. if you convert that into a bitstream or even just a simple coordinate offset, it doesn't look like random noise. \n\nit feels like a handshake protocol. like they're pinging each other to verify position or sync a clock without using standard radio frequencies that we can intercept. if this isn't just engine firings, can you look at the sequence again? if those delta values were actually a way of encoding a simple signal, what kind of pattern would you expect to see?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
